WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.680
If you take three different measurements of a single quantum particle and you chain them together so that they loop back to your starting point, the universe will hand you a mathematical receipt proving that the numbers you learned in grade school literally do not exist.

00:15.820 --> 00:20.000
Yeah, it's a genuinely staggering realization when you really sit with it.

00:20.040 --> 00:21.300
I mean, I'm not being metaphorical here.

00:21.300 --> 00:30.100
The physical universe actively rejects the basic real numbers that we use to, you know, balance our checkbooks or measure a piece of wood.

00:30.380 --> 00:34.940
Right, because we're so used to the idea that physics is built on top of math.

00:35.220 --> 00:41.320
Like, we assume math is just this passive language we use to describe a reality that is already sitting there fully formed.

00:41.440 --> 00:42.840
Yeah, like it's just a tape measure.

00:42.940 --> 00:43.280
Exactly.

00:43.540 --> 00:47.400
But when you look closely at quantum mechanics, the relationship is almost inverted.

00:47.400 --> 00:49.900
The math isn't just describing reality.

00:50.060 --> 00:58.120
The structural logic of the math is actively forcing reality to behave in ways that seem, well, utterly bizarre to human intuition.

00:58.420 --> 01:01.300
And that is exactly what we're getting into today.

