It really is, because the premise asks a profoundly simple question.

01:39.580 --> 01:45.820
It asks, what if quantum mechanics isn't just a bizarre set of magical, arbitrary rules handed down by a quirky universe?

01:45.820 --> 01:54.820
What if it's actually the only mathematically logical way to process probabilities and process missing information without creating literal logical paradoxes?

01:54.820 --> 01:59.980
I love this, because whenever you take a physics class, they usually just drop these massive, heavy equations on you.

