But the Kronecker product

34:36.740 --> 34:38.480
is just a mathematical convention.

34:38.920 --> 34:41.380
It's a choice of how to represent the combination.

34:41.720 --> 34:42.300
Okay, I'm listening.

34:42.700 --> 34:44.100
I feel like I'm being tricked by math again.

34:44.500 --> 34:45.620
Well, we have to ask

34:45.620 --> 34:47.240
what a complex number actually is.

34:47.500 --> 34:49.580
Chapter 19 introduces a concept

34:49.580 --> 34:51.240
popularized by Tristan Needham

34:51.240 --> 34:52.520
called the amplitwist.

34:52.520 --> 34:54.520
When you multiply a state

34:54.520 --> 34:55.640
by a complex number,

34:56.140 --> 34:58.820
you are doing two geometric operations simultaneously.

34:59.360 --> 35:00.540
You are scaling the amplitude,

35:00.720 --> 35:01.180
stretching it,

35:01.260 --> 35:02.380
and you are rotating it,

35:02.460 --> 35:03.360
or twisting it,

35:03.420 --> 35:03.860
in a plane.

35:03.940 --> 35:04.700
Scaling and twisting.

35:05.220 --> 35:05.920
The amplitwist.

35:06.180 --> 35:07.840
That matrix J we kept talking about,

35:07.940 --> 35:09.080
the missing real dimension,

35:09.240 --> 35:10.540
the anti-symmetric matrix,

35:10.740 --> 35:11.400
it is mathematically

35:11.400 --> 35:12.680
just a quarter turn rotation,

35:13.280 --> 35:14.740
R of pi over 2.

35:14.940 --> 35:16.900
It is the imaginary number I.

35:16.900 --> 35:18.680
It is literally just the concept

35:18.680 --> 35:19.920
of a 90-degree twist,

35:20.040 --> 35:22.220
but written out as a real 2x2 matrix

35:22.220 --> 35:24.220
instead of the single complex letter.

35:24.720 --> 35:25.920
Wait, so a complex number

35:25.920 --> 35:27.720
is just a 2D real matrix

35:27.720 --> 35:28.500
wearing a trench coat?

35:28.780 --> 35:29.760
Essentially, yes.

35:30.220 --> 35:32.160
Now, here is where the breakdown happened

35:32.160 --> 35:33.240
in our earlier test.

35:33.700 --> 35:35.220
When you combine systems

35:35.220 --> 35:36.440
using standard math,

35:36.880 --> 35:38.480
the traditional tensor product

35:38.480 --> 35:39.900
forces you to decide

35:39.900 --> 35:41.240
which local subsystem

35:41.240 --> 35:42.640
carries the global phase,

35:42.740 --> 35:43.360
the rotation.

35:43.840 --> 35:45.620
It forces one particle

35:45.620 --> 35:47.080
to quote-unquote

35:47.080 --> 35:48.340
hold the twist.

35:48.880 --> 35:50.360
This creates a redundancy,

35:50.620 --> 35:51.820
an artificial rigidity.

35:52.220 --> 35:54.140
And if we fix that redundancy...

35:54.140 --> 35:54.960
If you quotient out

35:54.960 --> 35:56.280
that gauge redundancy,

35:56.480 --> 35:58.000
which is a fancy mathematical way

35:58.000 --> 35:59.860
of saying you redistribute the phase

35:59.860 --> 36:01.180
across the whole tensor product

36:01.180 --> 36:02.280
so it doesn't matter who holds it,

36:02.700 --> 36:03.680
the ambiguity changes.

36:04.520 --> 36:06.320
The obstruction we found earlier

36:06.320 --> 36:07.280
wasn't in the physics

36:07.280 --> 36:07.860
of the universe,

36:08.060 --> 36:09.060
it was an artifact

36:09.060 --> 36:10.680
of our clumsy notation.

36:10.680 --> 36:11.260
Oh my god.

36:11.620 --> 36:12.740
It's exactly like looking

36:12.740 --> 36:13.960
at a Mercator projection map

36:13.960 --> 36:14.320
of the Earth.

36:14.320 --> 36:16.260
If you look at a standard classroom map,

36:16.500 --> 36:17.980
Greenland looks absolutely massive,

36:18.140 --> 36:18.700
almost as big

36:18.700 --> 36:20.180
as the entire continent of Africa.

36:20.380 --> 36:21.260
But that distortion

36:21.260 --> 36:22.780
is an artifact of the map,

36:23.060 --> 36:24.100
not the actual planet.

36:24.480 --> 36:25.620
You took a 3D globe

36:25.620 --> 36:27.540
and forced it onto a 2D grid,

36:27.760 --> 36:29.160
and the math of that projection

36:29.160 --> 36:31.320
created a fake, giant Greenland.

36:32.260 --> 36:33.580
Complex numbers might just be

36:33.580 --> 36:34.660
the easiest, cleanest,

36:34.760 --> 36:36.020
most natural globe to read,

36:36.260 --> 36:37.580
while real numbers require

36:37.580 --> 36:38.320
a super-convoluted,

36:39.220 --> 36:40.120
highly distorted,

36:40.320 --> 36:41.080
quotiented map

36:41.080 --> 36:43.040
to show the exact same Earth

36:43.040 --> 36:43.860
without breaking.

36:43.860 --> 36:45.460
That analogy is flawless.

36:46.040 --> 36:47.040
What's fascinating here

36:47.040 --> 36:48.640
is that the math confirms this.

36:49.300 --> 36:50.000
Complex numbers

36:50.000 --> 36:51.480
are an incredibly efficient

36:51.480 --> 36:52.540
bookkeeping device

36:52.540 --> 36:53.400
for handling this

36:53.400 --> 36:54.480
simultaneous rotation

36:54.480 --> 36:55.060
and scaling

36:55.060 --> 36:56.220
without creating

36:56.220 --> 36:57.580
fake topological holes.

36:57.820 --> 36:58.080
But,

36:58.480 --> 36:59.480
and this is a massive but,

36:59.900 --> 37:00.640
the deep dive

37:00.640 --> 37:01.580
asks a critical,

37:01.740 --> 37:02.840
unresolved question here.

37:02.880 --> 37:03.320
Which is?

37:03.580 --> 37:04.400
Does this new,

37:04.540 --> 37:05.480
highly convoluted,

37:05.520 --> 37:06.920
real tensor product,

37:07.060 --> 37:07.800
this fixed map,

37:08.120 --> 37:09.180
actually survive

37:09.180 --> 37:10.380
the local tomography tests

37:10.380 --> 37:11.020
we did earlier?

37:11.020 --> 37:12.420
Can it actually describe

37:12.420 --> 37:13.260
a joint state

37:13.260 --> 37:14.720
using only local measurements

37:14.720 --> 37:15.480
without inventing

37:15.480 --> 37:16.760
new, weird rules?

37:17.180 --> 37:18.160
The book leaves that

37:18.160 --> 37:19.260
explicitly unresolved.

37:19.360 --> 37:20.100
So it's still a mystery.

37:20.360 --> 37:20.780
It is.

37:21.220 --> 37:22.580
It proves that real QM

37:22.580 --> 37:24.040
can mimic complex QM

37:24.040 --> 37:25.320
if you drastically change

37:25.320 --> 37:26.940
the rules of how things compose,

37:27.280 --> 37:28.280
but it doesn't prove

37:28.280 --> 37:29.280
that this new rule

37:29.280 --> 37:29.920
of composition

37:29.920 --> 37:31.320
is forced by the same

37:31.320 --> 37:32.440
elegant, pure logic

37:32.440 --> 37:33.160
we started with.

37:33.280 --> 37:33.540
Wow.

37:33.800 --> 37:34.720
So complex numbers

37:34.720 --> 37:35.580
might not be magic,

37:35.740 --> 37:36.300
they might just be

37:36.300 --> 37:37.700
the universe's best shorthand.

37:37.700 --> 37:40.380
But we have one last stop

37:40.380 --> 37:41.080
on this journey.

37:41.460 --> 37:42.040
We've talked a lot

37:42.040 --> 37:42.720
about dimensions

37:42.720 --> 37:43.840
and graph structures

37:43.840 --> 37:44.520
and cycles.

37:44.760 --> 37:45.580
If we pull back

37:45.580 --> 37:46.440
to the big picture

37:46.440 --> 37:48.140
of these context graphs

37:48.140 --> 37:49.280
and probability loops,

37:49.680 --> 37:50.540
I want to know

37:50.540 --> 37:52.400
exactly when reality breaks.

37:52.740 --> 37:53.860
Is it a gradual fade

37:53.860 --> 37:55.040
into quantum weirdness

37:55.040 --> 37:56.280
as things get more complex

37:56.280 --> 37:57.860
or is it a sudden snap?

37:58.140 --> 37:59.380
This is directly addressed

37:59.380 --> 38:00.320
in chapter 20

38:00.320 --> 38:01.180
and chapter 23.

38:01.640 --> 38:02.320
Let's look at what

38:02.320 --> 38:03.000
Flyxion calls

38:03.000 --> 38:03.760
minimal witnesses

38:03.760 --> 38:04.760
in higher dimensions.

38:05.360 --> 38:06.240
Back in our two

38:06.240 --> 38:07.120
outcome systems,

38:07.260 --> 38:07.400
you know,

38:07.520 --> 38:08.160
d equals 2,

38:08.240 --> 38:08.700
we established

38:08.700 --> 38:09.680
we needed a triangle,

38:09.900 --> 38:10.580
a closed loop,

38:10.640 --> 38:11.920
to break real QM.

38:12.040 --> 38:12.240
Right.

38:12.340 --> 38:13.020
The Betty numbered

38:13.020 --> 38:14.480
beta 1 had to be 1.

38:14.640 --> 38:15.000
Exactly.

38:15.260 --> 38:16.480
But chapter 20 proves

38:16.480 --> 38:17.060
that if you move

38:17.060 --> 38:17.540
to a system

38:17.540 --> 38:18.880
with three or more outcomes,

38:19.060 --> 38:19.760
d greater than

38:19.760 --> 38:20.520
or equal to 3,

38:20.900 --> 38:21.820
the minimal witness

38:21.820 --> 38:23.440
collapses to a single edge.

38:23.740 --> 38:25.800
Meaning beta 1 equals 0.

38:26.280 --> 38:27.400
You don't even need cycles

38:27.400 --> 38:28.300
to break real quantum

38:28.300 --> 38:29.020
mechanics anymore.

38:29.500 --> 38:30.560
A single transition,

38:30.720 --> 38:32.340
like that 3x3 DFT matrix

38:32.340 --> 38:33.420
we talked about an hour ago,

38:33.460 --> 38:34.760
is enough to instantly

38:34.760 --> 38:36.200
demand complex numbers.

38:36.400 --> 38:36.660
Yes.

38:37.080 --> 38:38.260
But chapter 23

38:38.260 --> 38:39.920
asks the density question

38:39.920 --> 38:41.660
specifically for d equals 2

38:41.660 --> 38:43.140
where single edges are safe.

38:43.520 --> 38:44.420
It asks,

38:44.700 --> 38:45.700
is there an erides

38:45.700 --> 38:46.680
reni threshold?

38:47.260 --> 38:47.860
What is that?

38:47.940 --> 38:48.760
I haven't heard that term.

38:48.860 --> 38:49.700
In graph theory,

38:49.840 --> 38:51.060
it's a critical density

38:51.060 --> 38:51.780
where the behavior

38:51.780 --> 38:52.440
of a network

38:52.440 --> 38:54.120
suddenly and drastically changes.

38:54.780 --> 38:55.600
Think of how water

38:55.600 --> 38:56.920
gradually cools down,

38:57.020 --> 38:58.180
but then at exactly

38:58.180 --> 38:59.020
zero degrees,

38:59.200 --> 39:00.420
it suddenly phase changes

39:00.420 --> 39:01.360
into solid ice.

39:01.580 --> 39:02.200
Oh, okay.

39:02.340 --> 39:03.580
Do these probability graphs

39:03.580 --> 39:04.920
gradually become harder

39:04.920 --> 39:06.560
to realize with real numbers

39:06.560 --> 39:07.860
as you randomly add

39:07.860 --> 39:08.880
more and more connections?

39:09.080 --> 39:09.680
And what is the result?

39:09.760 --> 39:11.040
Does it bend before it breaks?

39:11.160 --> 39:13.200
The result is terrifyingly sharp.

39:13.640 --> 39:14.940
There is no gradual transition.

39:15.500 --> 39:16.180
Under independent

39:16.180 --> 39:17.600
continuous edge measures,

39:17.780 --> 39:19.520
meaning if you randomly assign

39:19.520 --> 39:20.440
valid probabilities

39:20.440 --> 39:21.260
to the connections,

39:21.780 --> 39:23.560
the very moment a graph

39:23.560 --> 39:25.500
has even one single cycle.

39:25.600 --> 39:26.440
The moment it loops.

39:26.440 --> 39:28.300
The moment beta 1

39:28.300 --> 39:29.460
is greater than

39:29.460 --> 39:30.780
or equal to 1,

39:31.340 --> 39:32.100
the probability

39:32.100 --> 39:33.360
of that entire network

39:33.360 --> 39:34.920
working with real numbers

39:34.920 --> 39:37.000
drops to exactly zero.

39:37.300 --> 39:38.400
It is measure zero.

39:38.460 --> 39:38.700
Wait, wait.

39:38.760 --> 39:39.840
So it's not like a bridge

39:39.840 --> 39:40.920
groaning under the weight

39:40.920 --> 39:41.460
of traffic,

39:41.640 --> 39:42.420
gradually bowing

39:42.420 --> 39:43.460
until it finally collapses.

39:44.060 --> 39:44.960
You're saying the bridge

39:44.960 --> 39:46.800
is structurally flawless,

39:47.280 --> 39:48.280
mathematically perfect

39:48.280 --> 39:49.320
in real numbers,

39:49.460 --> 39:50.760
right up until you connect

39:50.760 --> 39:51.800
the very last bolt

39:51.800 --> 39:52.900
that forms a closed loop,

39:53.300 --> 39:54.520
and then the entire thing

39:54.520 --> 39:55.940
instantly vaporizes

39:55.940 --> 39:57.680
into mathematical impossibility.

39:58.100 --> 39:58.540
Precisely.

39:58.940 --> 40:00.200
It is what mathematicians

40:00.200 --> 40:01.960
call a co-dimension 1 event.

40:02.100 --> 40:02.960
Wait, co-dimension 1?

40:03.000 --> 40:04.200
What does that actually mean visually?

40:04.340 --> 40:05.440
Imagine a massive

40:05.440 --> 40:06.720
three-dimensional room.

40:07.460 --> 40:08.540
A co-dimension 1 object

40:08.540 --> 40:10.100
is a two-dimensional plane,

40:10.280 --> 40:11.200
like a sheet of paper,

40:11.480 --> 40:12.320
infinitely thin,

40:12.440 --> 40:13.440
cutting through that room.

40:13.900 --> 40:15.220
It has zero volume

40:15.220 --> 40:16.480
compared to the room itself.

40:16.900 --> 40:17.800
If you throw a dart

40:17.800 --> 40:18.820
completely randomly

40:18.820 --> 40:19.580
into that room,

40:19.680 --> 40:20.840
the mathematical probability

40:20.840 --> 40:21.700
of the tip of the dart

40:21.700 --> 40:23.180
hitting that incredibly thin plane

40:23.180 --> 40:24.380
is precisely zero.

40:24.720 --> 40:25.720
So a universe governed

40:25.720 --> 40:26.800
by real numbers

40:26.800 --> 40:28.660
is that infinitely thin

40:28.660 --> 40:29.380
sheet of paper,

40:29.660 --> 40:30.540
and the space

40:30.540 --> 40:32.200
of all possible quantum states

40:32.200 --> 40:33.760
is the massive room.

40:34.240 --> 40:35.200
The moment you close a loop,

40:35.580 --> 40:36.840
you realize you are in the room,

40:37.060 --> 40:37.880
not on the paper.

40:37.880 --> 40:38.320
Exactly.

40:38.720 --> 40:40.320
It is not an asymptotic limit

40:40.320 --> 40:41.140
where things just get

40:41.140 --> 40:42.120
harder to calculate.

40:42.680 --> 40:44.340
The threshold of impossibility

40:44.340 --> 40:45.600
is crossed completely

40:45.600 --> 40:46.920
at the very first cycle.

40:47.440 --> 40:48.840
It proves that realizability

40:48.840 --> 40:49.760
over real numbers

40:49.760 --> 40:50.740
is not generic.

40:51.200 --> 40:52.940
It is the ultimate rare exception.

40:52.940 --> 40:54.480
The moment you close

40:54.480 --> 40:55.400
a loop of information,

40:55.900 --> 40:57.500
real numbers evaporate.

40:57.500 --> 40:58.420
This has been

40:58.420 --> 40:59.660
an absolute journey

40:59.660 --> 41:00.380
to try and summarize

41:00.380 --> 41:01.420
what we've just done.

41:01.540 --> 41:02.520
We started with

41:02.520 --> 41:04.280
bare classical probabilities,

41:04.560 --> 41:05.580
a simple mixing of paint.

41:05.740 --> 41:05.820
Yeah.

41:06.080 --> 41:07.420
We saw how linking

41:07.420 --> 41:08.340
those probabilities

41:08.340 --> 41:08.960
in cycles

41:08.960 --> 41:10.800
created geometrical paradoxes

41:10.800 --> 41:12.060
like the Escher staircase

41:12.060 --> 41:13.420
of the triangle gluing theorem.

41:13.820 --> 41:15.260
We mathematically proved

41:15.260 --> 41:16.280
that entanglement

41:16.280 --> 41:17.100
isn't necessarily

41:17.100 --> 41:18.660
an intrinsic physical property

41:18.660 --> 41:19.240
of a particle,

41:19.560 --> 41:20.880
but might actually be relative

41:20.880 --> 41:21.800
to the math you used

41:21.800 --> 41:22.460
to describe it.

41:22.540 --> 41:23.520
The magic eye poster.

41:23.860 --> 41:24.100
Right.

41:24.520 --> 41:25.720
We derived the famous

41:25.720 --> 41:26.660
Schrodinger equation

41:26.660 --> 41:27.920
not from assuming

41:27.920 --> 41:29.220
physical energy exists,

41:29.540 --> 41:30.800
but from pure logic

41:30.800 --> 41:32.940
and continuous reversible time.

41:33.280 --> 41:34.380
And we realized

41:34.380 --> 41:35.500
that complex numbers

41:35.500 --> 41:36.980
might just be nature's

41:36.980 --> 41:38.620
most efficient bookkeeping tool

41:38.620 --> 41:39.980
for a universe made of

41:39.980 --> 41:41.720
twisting scaling probabilities.

41:42.020 --> 41:43.200
It strips quantum mechanics

41:43.200 --> 41:44.560
of its arbitrary mystique.

41:44.800 --> 41:45.640
It takes away the feeling

41:45.640 --> 41:46.240
that the universe

41:46.240 --> 41:47.280
is just mocking us

41:47.280 --> 41:48.220
with weird rules

41:48.220 --> 41:49.160
and replaces it

41:49.160 --> 41:50.580
with something even more profound.

41:51.560 --> 41:52.760
Structural inevitability.

41:53.400 --> 41:53.960
Quantum mechanics

41:53.960 --> 41:55.360
is simply the only way

41:55.360 --> 41:56.800
the puddle pieces fit together.

41:57.040 --> 41:57.820
Which leaves us

41:57.820 --> 41:58.540
with a final,

41:58.960 --> 42:00.300
very provocative thought.

42:00.700 --> 42:00.840
Right.

42:00.860 --> 42:01.960
If you are listening to this,

42:02.040 --> 42:03.040
I want you to seriously

42:03.040 --> 42:03.720
ponder this

42:03.720 --> 42:04.680
as you go about your day.

42:04.980 --> 42:05.740
We've just spent

42:05.740 --> 42:06.900
this entire deep dive

42:06.900 --> 42:07.820
seeing how almost

42:07.820 --> 42:09.200
all of quantum mechanics

42:09.200 --> 42:10.260
can be derived

42:10.260 --> 42:11.520
as a forced requirement

42:11.520 --> 42:12.560
of processing

42:12.560 --> 42:13.440
missing information

42:13.440 --> 42:14.560
without creating

42:14.560 --> 42:15.640
logical contradictions.

42:16.100 --> 42:17.180
So does the wave function

42:17.180 --> 42:18.520
actually exist out there

42:18.520 --> 42:19.360
in the physical world?

42:19.360 --> 42:21.320
That's the million dollar question.

42:21.800 --> 42:22.720
Is there a physical

42:22.720 --> 42:23.980
undulating wave

42:23.980 --> 42:25.360
of energy guiding particles?

42:26.060 --> 42:26.960
Or is the universe

42:26.960 --> 42:28.480
entirely made of pure math

42:28.480 --> 42:29.180
and information?

42:29.620 --> 42:30.380
And quantum mechanics

42:30.380 --> 42:32.160
is just the only possible software

42:32.160 --> 42:32.780
our brains

42:32.780 --> 42:33.880
and our instruments can use

42:33.880 --> 42:35.160
to render a reality

42:35.160 --> 42:35.980
where we don't have

42:35.980 --> 42:36.560
all the facts.

42:37.040 --> 42:38.020
Is the physical world

42:38.020 --> 42:39.420
just the gears we can't see?

42:39.800 --> 42:40.520
And quantum mechanics

42:40.520 --> 42:41.740
is just the inevitable blur

42:41.740 --> 42:42.340
of the machinery.

42:43.000 --> 42:43.620
Think about it.

42:43.840 --> 42:44.400
We'll catch you

42:44.400 --> 42:45.380
on the next deep dive.

42:45.380 --> 42:59.280
We'll catch you

42:59.320 --> 43:00.900
in the next video.

